<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>marimo WebAssembly + GitHub Pages Template</title>
  <!-- Include Tailwind CSS via CDN -->
  <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
</head>
<body class="font-sans text-gray-800 bg-white p-5">    
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <header>
      <div class="container">
        <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center my-4">Data Visualization Principles</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">What is visualizing data?</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="font-sans text-gray-800 bg-white p-5">
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center my-4">Be clear about what you're showing</h1>
        <p>Labels, units, filters, views</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Labels</li>
          <li>units</li>
          <li>filters</li>
          <li>Purpose</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center my-4">Accuracy Matters</h1>
        <p>Make sure your data are correct</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Don't guess at ratios/charts</li>
          <li>Know your underlying data</li>
          <li>Double check your data</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center my-4">Everything can encode data</h1>
        <p>Combinations to represent different layers of data</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Color</li>
          <li>Shape</li>
          <li>Size</li>
          <li>Motion</li>
          <li>Sound</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center my-4">Visualizations should fit the data</h1>
      <p><em>Use the right visualization for the kind of data that you’re working with</em></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Events – Scatterplot</li>
        <li>Counts – Bar charts, histogram</li>
        <li>Proportions – Stacked bar, pie</li>
        <li>Time series – Line charts</li>
      </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center my-4">Keep the Context Clear</h1>
      <p><em>Always keep a sign of the data filters/manipulations that have been applied</em></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Filters</li>
        <li>Sorts</li>
        <li>Types</li>
      </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center my-4">Choose Scales Wisely</h1>
      <p><em>A scale should show the range of all possible values and relative/relevant values</em></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Color scales</li>
        <li>Time scales</li>
        <li>Geo-ranges</li>
      </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center my-4">Dashboards are not Reports</h1>
      <p><em>A report offers a snapshot, a dashboard helps a user build their own snapshot.</em></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Reports are read, dashboards are used</li>
        <li>The primary task for the dashboard should be immediately apparent</li>
        <li>If there are multiple tasks, filters should persist between them as much as possible</li>
      </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center my-4">Give the reader a headline</h1>
      <p><em>The big number is all that most users will read</em></p>
      <ul>
        <li>A big number should be essential, actionable, and relevant to decisions</li>
        <li>Top and left within each component</li>
        <li>Support numbers with graphs or context</li>
      </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center my-4">Scan then read</h1>
      <p><em>Prioritize the headline, lead in to the story</em></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Headlines should always be actionable</li>
        <li>Use the z-pattern</li>
        <li>Use tasks to balance density of visualizations with density of data</li>
      </ul>
      </div>
      
    </main>
</body>
</html>